changes.change:
Before deep training, run a read-only audit and show only measured numbers on the training page and in the log:
- files with denoise applied (sources.json denoised, snr_before) and with vocals separated;
- force-cut clips (forced_cuts > 0) in the train split;
- lines without final punctuation;
- lines containing English, with their English word counts;
- questions in train and in val;
- rows still flagged suspect;
- clips whose precise-ensemble similarity to the voice centroid is an outlier (median − 3.5·MAD). These are reported only, never dropped, for the teacher to listen to.
If any training clip comes from a source with denoised=True and separated=False, and the original video still exists, re-render those clips in place: ffmpeg extract (prepare.extract_audio) → 60 Hz high-pass → same −20 LUFS gain, no denoise → cut the manifest's [start, end] (prepare.py L262-266) → overwrite clips/<id>.wav after a backup. Clip ids, texts and splits are untouched, so there is no re-slicing and the 138 hand repairs are kept.

VoiceTwin ships its own 1A script, run with the bundle's Python (cwd = GPT-SoVITS root, same env as the official 1A). For each train.list line it reproduces inference's zh path exactly:
- re.sub(' {2,}', ' '), then LangSegmenter.getTexts(text);
- merge consecutive en segments and consecutive non-en segments, labelling non-en as 'zh' (TextPreprocessor abe9843 else-branch L163-175);
- per segment, the official clean_text(seg.replace('%','-').replace('￥',','), lang, version);
- BERT for zh segments with the same chinese-roberta hidden_states[-3:-2] code as 1-get-text.py L56-84; zeros(1024, len(phones)) for en segments (as get_bert_inf L212-222);
- concatenate phones, word2ph and norm_text, then write 2-name2text-0.txt as name\tphones\tword2ph\tnorm_text and 3-bert/<name>.pt with shape[-1] == len(phones). The s1 dataset asserts this (AR/data/dataset.py L222-231); s2 reads only the phones column (module/data_utils.py tmp[1]).
Lines with no CJK use the en path. That is the same rule synthesis should use for text_lang: zh whenever CJK > 0. It also fixes the separately confirmed detect_lang 'en' bug.
Self-check inside the script: for the first 30 lines without Latin letters, the phones must equal clean_text(line,'zh'), i.e. the official result; otherwise exit 3. On any failure (import error, exception, exit ≠ 0, or fewer than 98 % of lines written), VoiceTwin deletes the partial output, logs a Chinese reason and runs the official 1-get-text.py.

Run 1A, 1B (2-get-hubert-wav32k.py), SV (2-get-sv.py) and 1C (3-get-semantic.py) as two concurrent processes on GPU 0 (i_part 0/1, all_parts 2), as the official webui does with gpu_numbers '0-0'. Merge 2-name2text-{i}.txt and 6-name2semantic-{i}.tsv; 1B and SV write per-file .pt and need no merge. Then count:
- rows in 2-name2text and 6-name2semantic;
- files in 4-cnhubert, 5-wav32k and 7-sv_cn against the N expected;
- from the logs: s2 'total left: N', 'skipped_phone', 'skipped_dur' and 'load audio or ssl error' (module/data_utils.py); s1 'dataset.__len__():' and 'deleted N audios who's phoneme/sec…' (AR/data/dataset.py L140-170).
Report 「实际参加训练：音色 X 条、语气 Y 条（共 N 条）」 (measured) and warn in Chinese with the reason when either is below 98 %.

