changes.change:
Per-sentence constant gain:
- L_i = speech-only loudness of the chosen sentence;
- d_i = L_i − median(L);
- d′_i = clip(d_i · min(1, σ_her / σ_gen), her p05, p95);
- the gain applied to the sentence is d′_i − d_i dB.
Then the global level is matched to her source LUFS as today. If a sentence would exceed −1 dBFS, a lookahead limiter (5 ms lookahead, 50 ms release, gain <= 1) is applied to THAT sentence only.
The report shows measured values: 「句子之间的音量差：你本人 ±a dB；这次 ±b dB；整篇响度 c LUFS（目标 d）」.

Twin parameters for trim_edges, taken from her measured onset/offset (change 1 e):
- tail threshold = max(floor + 12, speech95 − 45, −70) dB, where floor is the candidate's own 3rd-percentile frame dB;
- tail pad = clip(her median offset decay, 30, 120) ms;
- fades keep the same shape, and the first and last samples are 0.
Breaths are kept only if 30% or more of her clips have one before the onset (her recordings are described as silent between sentences, so the default stays 'removed').
Twin scores the trimmed, delivered audio.

Twin mode of select_and_calibrate.
- Items: validation clips (30 after the training-side change).
- Per (checkpoint, item): 3 seeds (1234, 4321, 9876), the twin reference matcher excluding the item, aux alternating 3 and 0, the current speed calibration.
- Per item, compared with her real recording of the same sentence:
  - two-sided saturating pct (change 2) instead of cos/p50;
  - F0 contour correlation after DTW (librosa.sequence.dtw on 20 MFCCs, semitone F0 along the path);
  - duration ratio;
  - inner-pause position agreement;
  - LTAS distance to that clip;
  - CER.
- Checkpoint score = mean over items of the best-of-3 seeds, which mirrors best-of-N generation.
- Winner by a paired bootstrap over items (1000 resamples). If the CI includes 0, log 「差别在误差范围内」 and keep the higher mean.
- Failed syntheses count as the worst score instead of being skipped.
- Speed calibration comes from the winner under these conditions.

