judges.best_ideas:
Keep (verified against the code):

1. Mixed zh/en training front end (model design), with self-check, fallback to the official 1A, and a stamp that covers the front end. 559/1004 lines and 2080 English words (6.1% of syllables) are deleted today by chinese2.replace_punctuation during training, while inference keeps them.

2. text_lang / prompt_lang = 'zh' whenever the text has any CJK character (all three designs). Verified bug: detect_lang returns 'en' when cjk < 0.2·words, and the 'en' path passes the whole text to English g2p, so the Chinese words are not spoken. Add send_lang to the cache key.

3. Several candidates per real api_v2 request (search design):
   - N copies joined with '\n', cut0, batch_size=N, parallel_infer, speed 1.0001 to force per-fragment VITS (verified in both real TTS.py versions, no resampling for L<10001);
   - strict exact-zero split with fallback to single requests (the replica 1004/1004 OK; short texts merge, so they need single requests);
   - auto-tune B on measured candidates/s, which also catches Windows VRAM spill;
   - on OOM (200 + 1 s of 16 kHz silence + traceback), halve B before the existing fatal path.
   Use it in checkpoint selection too.

4. Producer thread plus scoring cascade (quick single SV member, then the full 3-model judge + ASR on the top 12) so the GPU never waits for CPU scoring. The cancel Event is global, so this is thread-safe.

5. Training resource squeeze (model design):
   - batch probe that watches nvidia-smi peak memory and throughput (spill detection), then an OOM ladder stepping down one at a time;
   - 2-part feature extraction as the official '0-0';
   - measured GPU utilization and per-phase timings stored for later ETAs;
   - audit of how many clips were actually trained (s2 'total left', s1 dataset length);
   - disk guard.

6. Keep her current 30.6-minute model as a competitor. Deep selection over all saved checkpoints with several seeds and 一模一样 generation conditions (aux, matched references); a failed synthesis counts as the worst score; a bootstrap tie keeps the top 2 for per-sentence choice. Recalibrate speed under these conditions.

7. Reference bank from train-split clips (3.2-9.8 s after trimming; the api requires 3-10 s). Per-sentence shortlist by kind, continuous length, English share and a measured prior. Only the final chunk of a long question uses a question reference.

8. Mixed CER: Paraformer on the CJK part, Whisper on the English words, counting deletions and substitutions only.

9. Consensus timbre (mean − 0.5·spread, capped at her natural p90). Minimum candidates plus a plateau stopping rule. Store the top-K candidates so a redo continues the search, and re-rank stored candidates when the judge changes.

10. Perception pieces that stay within the rules:
   - pauses re-measured on raw/<sid>.wav, then measure-and-correct layout (still exact zeros);
   - prosody-contour z-scores, with the weight set only by validation calibration;
   - Viterbi continuity across neighbouring sentences;
   - same-seed tempo refinement, kept as one more candidate.

11. The default (model design's precise version):
   - 'auto', empty or missing → 一模一样 on every tier;
   - an old config is detected by the exact v0.1.0-v0.1.3 line 'quality: balanced # fast（每句 1 个候选）…' and treated as auto;
   - a genuinely hand-edited value is honoured and shown in Chinese;
   - the radio is reset on every page load (radio default value='identical' and the do_generate fallback changed from 'balanced');
   - the CLI default is identical;
   - the training page radio defaults to 一模一样;
   - weaker machines keep the default with smaller caps, a measured ETA and the suggestion 「着急可改选均衡」.

12. Final '，' for the 112 mid-sentence clips (low risk; train.list only).
